  "protocol": "Isolated Release Metal server per run, one slot, fixed 8192 MiB ledger, 4096 context and logical batch, target microbatch 8, BF16 KV, compact Q4_0 DFlash2 (BF16 selectors), depth 3, draft microbatch 128. The warmup uses the last eight archive IDs with eight outputs. Then POST the original 912 handover IDs, uncached, greedy (seed 42), ignore EOS, stream 64 IDs. Client monotonic TTFT goes to the first token-bearing SSE event. TPS is 63 divided by elapsed seconds from first to last token-bearing event. One clean timing on the final binary and a separate one-line shape check. OS file cache uncontrolled. Comparisons use existing records.",
